// Forces / torque on the rotating bob (inner wall).
// Pattern: the pimpleFoam/RAS/propeller tutorial's system/forces.
// rhoInf is the density (incompressible): forces come out in Newtons,
// moments in N.m. The moment is taken about CofR = the origin, which
// lies on the cylinder axis (X), so the X component of the moment is
// the torque about the axis of rotation.
//
// This is the SECTOR torque (4 deg wedge slice, 1 mm axial slice).
// couette_post.py scales it to the full cylinder:
//   T_full = M_x * (360/4) * (0.060/0.001) = M_x * 5400

forces
{
    type            forces;
    libs            (forces);

    writeControl    timeStep;
    writeInterval   5;
    log             true;

    patches         (innerWall);
    rho             rhoInf;
    rhoInf          1000;

    CofR            (0 0 0);
}


